Description: Close a popped-out AdwDialog when its parent window is destroyed
 gtk-nocsd presents an AdwDialog in a window of its own, transient for and
 modal over the parent window, and adds the parent's application and window
 as the dialog's "app" and "win" action groups. When the parent window is
 destroyed, the dialog window stays a toplevel and keeps the dialog, the
 parent window and the application alive. Without gtk-nocsd the dialog is
 embedded in the parent window and goes with it.
 .
 Epiphany, quit with SIGTERM while its "Set as Default Browser?" dialog is
 open, then still holds its EphyShell after g_application_run returns and
 aborts on g_assert (!ephy_shell).
 .
 When a dialog is presented on a parent window, connect to the parent's
 "unrealize" (once per parent and dialog, until the dialog goes). If the
 parent is no longer among the toplevel windows, that is, it was destroyed
 and not just unrealized, and the dialog is still in a window transient for
 it, close the dialog: "closed" is emitted once, even when can-close is
 FALSE, and can-close is restored afterwards.
